      q: "A 34-year-old woman who recently emigrated from Russia comes to the physician due to weakness, exertional dyspnea, and orthopnea. On cardiac auscultation, a snap followed by a rumbling diastolic murmur is heard over the cardiac apex. The snap most likely occurs nearest to which of the following points on the cardiac pressure- volume loop?",
      a: ["A", "B", "C", "D", "E", "F"],
