      q: "A 44-year-old woman comes to the office for follow-up. The patient sustained a complete C7 spinal cord injury a year ago after falling off a cliff while hiking. She is able to move her shoulders and upper arms but has paraplegia and uses a wheelchair. The patient has a suprapubic catheter due to neurogenic bladder. She has no other medical conditions. She is a lifelong nonsmoker. Which of the following changes in respiratory parameters are most likely present in this patient?",
