      q: "A 22-year-old woman with no prenatal care has a normal vaginal delivery. On physical examination, the infant's external genitalia are atypical and ambiguous. There is an intermediate clitorophallic length and a perineal urethral opening. Well-circumscribed, mobile masses are palpable bilaterally in the inguinal area. Vital signs are normal. Serum testosterone level is within normal limits. A karyotype is performed and shows 46, XY. This infant most likely has a deficiency in which of the following enzymes?",
