      q: "A newborn boy is found to have a serum TSH above and serum thyroxine below the normal range for his age. The patient was born at 39 weeks gestation via spontaneous vaginal delivery. His mother has no medical conditions. On examination, the patient's length and weight are normal, and he has no apparent congenital abnormalities. Ultrasound of the neck shows a normal-sized thyroid gland in the appropriate location. Which of the following is the most likely cause of this patient's condition?",
