      q: "A 67-year-old man comes to the office with right tibial pain that started 3 months ago and has increased in intensity over time. He also has had progressive hearing impairment for the last year. Physical examination reveals local tenderness and a lumpy protuberance over the right tibia. After extensive evaluation, the patient undergoes a bone biopsy. The pathologist identifies numerous multinucleated cells, some containing over 100 nuclei. Which of the following factors is essential for the differentiation of the cells described by the pathologist?",
